# Ships templates/, static/, and locale/ in the SDIST — not .py files, so no build backend
# includes them by default (APP-DESIGN.md §2). Paired with include-package-data = true and
# [tool.setuptools.package-data] in pyproject.toml, which is what actually lands them in the
# WHEEL — this file alone is not enough, see that table's comment.
#
# templates/ matters more than usual for this app: Phase 6's Jazzmin admin lives there, so a
# MANIFEST.in gap here would silently ship an app whose admin page 404s on a fresh install.
recursive-include src/dynamic_user/templates *
recursive-include src/dynamic_user/static *
recursive-include src/dynamic_user/locale *.po *.mo
include src/dynamic_user/py.typed
